Platform: the pantherlake fixture with its NPU's PCI device id replaced by 0x1234,
an id intel_vpu could bind but intel-npu-plugin 0.37.1 npuIDs
(cmd/npu_plugin/npu_plugin.go) does not list. Not a real part: it exercises the
auto-detection path that skips an NPU the bundled plugin would not advertise.

Platform: Core Ultra Series 3 (Panther Lake) laptop: Xe3 iGPU on xe, NPU 5 on
intel_vpu, IAA on idxd with one user work queue, hybrid P/E cores, firmware
installed, one NUMA node.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- 0x8086 0xb080 "Panther Lake [Arc B390]": pci.ids 2026.10.15; INTEL_PTL_IDS in
  include/drm/intel/pciids.h.
- 0x8086 0xb03e NPU: drivers/accel/ivpu/ivpu_drv.h (PCI_DEVICE_ID_PTL_P); listed in
  intel-device-plugins v0.37.1 cmd/npu_plugin/npu_plugin.go; class 0x1200 per its
  NFD rule (deployments/nfd/overlays/node-feature-rules).
- accel0 and /dev/accel/accel0: Documentation/accel/introduction.rst.
- xe/ptl_guc_70.bin, intel/vpu/vpu_50xx_v1.bin: linux-firmware tag 20260916 WHENCE.
- IAA 0xb02d: drivers/dma/idxd/registers.h (PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_IAA_PTL, first in
  v6.14) and its entry in drivers/dma/idxd/init.c; iax<n>/wq<dev>.<n> naming and
  /dev/iax, /dev/char links as in xeon-spr-accel. PCI numa_node -1 and one
  node0: Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-pci, Documentation/ABI/stable/sysfs-devices-node.
- /sys/devices/cpu_core/cpus and cpu_atom/cpus: tools/perf/Documentation/intel-hybrid.txt.
- iGPU at 00:02.0, NPU at 00:0b.0: Intel client BDFs (the captured raptorlake-nvidia
  iGPU is at 00:02.0 too).

Layout: sysfs paths and relative symlinks follow the driver core's naming
(class devices under <pci dev>/<class>/<name>; /sys/class/<class>/<name> and
/sys/bus/pci/devices/<bdf> as relative links; <dev>/driver -> bus/pci/drivers/<drv>),
in exactly the form tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes (the matrix test re-captures
each tree and requires an identical result).

Not from hardware: the IAA BDF (00:0c.0), the char-device minor, the P/E CPU
numbering (4 P then 12 E/LP-E, contiguous), the kernel release string, and the
cpuinfo flags line.

CPU topology (G3/G4 in docs/intel-capability-map.md): 4 P (Cougar Cove, no SMT)
+ 8 E in two 4-core clusters + 4 LP E, the H-series 4+8+4 tile (Wikipedia
"Panther Lake (microprocessor)", core counts). PTL is hybrid_big_small in
arch/x86/events/intel/core.c, so LP E-cores are in cpu_atom. Not from hardware:
the cache/index*/ and topology/core_cpus_list files. The LP E-cores 12-15 carry no
L3 entry, as on the Meteor Lake and Arrow Lake LP island; that Panther Lake's
LP E-cores report no L3 is UNVERIFIED (no Panther Lake capture yet).
